rule:
rg21: bounded direct fence admission alone (L2) vs main. Beads br-9ott5 and br-kp1in.19. Written 2026-10-21 ~05:45Z,
before the L2-only build finished and before any rg21 run. It gets a FROZEN line with the cand sha before its first run.

DISCLOSED CONTEXT. Everything below was seen before this rule.
- ab18 (cand = SP + L2 + L3; base = main 2b5d14d7 + br-tsqvm fix, the same base binary as here), LOSS:
  - grant refusals per 1,000: P2 base 928.7 / cand 295.5; P6 base 766.4 / cand 2.3;
  - P2 completion 1.12x base;
  - P6 send p99 1.21x base;
  - smoke acked sends 0.77x and 0.84x of base;
  - cand soak convergence failed in both orders, while base passed.
  So the thresholds below were chosen with the SP+L2+L3 numbers in view. L2 alone has not been measured.
- rg19 (RG alone): LOSS, after 2 valid runs. The message reconciler's per-message verification under the fence is the long
  holder (br-9ott5).

LEVER: rc1020i = 2b5d14d7 + tsqvm_v1.patch + clippy rename + L2.
- L2 = admit_direct_publication: retry try_begin_repair with a doubling pause of at most 10 ms, for up to 500 ms, checking
  cancellation on every attempt. Plus its 3 unit tests, which pass on rc1020h (vrgl2 l2 6/6).
- Tree diff 8c8518bb7967 (l2only_tree_v1.patch). The reconciler file is untouched.

ARMS (portable release, same host, host lock):
- base = build36/ab18b_base/am, sha256 3d35263d06e664f345572b9175c7102d445ba6e87b0ccf11a1ca491f5401e254, re-run live;
- cand = build36/l2only_cand/am. The build log must show diff=8c8518bb7967. The sha256 is recorded at freeze.

RUNS: as rg19 (P2: base cand cand base base cand; P6: cand base base cand; smoke in both orders; same env and validity rules).

PRIMARY. Both must hold.
- M1 (reservations usable below saturation): pooled valid P6 cand file_reservation_paths errors <= 10 per 1,000 calls.
- M2 (partial relief at saturation): pooled valid P2 cand reservation error rate <= 50% of base's.

GUARDS (any failure = LOSS):
- G1: P2 completion median cand <= 1.05x base; smoke swarm acked sends cand >= 0.95x base in each order. This is not loosened
  for unequal work.
- G2:
  - non-reservation paced tool errors cand <= base + 5 (P2 and P6 pooled);
  - smoke tool errors cand <= base + 5 in each order;
  - cand crash phase PASS in each order;
  - integrity_check ok;
  - no canonical-id collision errors in any cand log;
  - smoke dispatch zombies for cand == 0 or <= base's, in each order (GH#351's symptom: L2 waits on request threads).
- G3: P6 send p99 and last-60 s send p90 cand <= 1.2x base; P6 file_reservation_paths p99 and release p99 cand <= base + 0.5 s;
  every P6 completion <= 330 s.
- G4: post-swarm un-archived cand <= base + 2% of cand's acked swarm sends, in each order. The smoke soak "archive converges after
  load stops" must not pass for base and fail for cand.
- C: on current main + L2, all of these:
  - storage lib nextest --no-fail-fast (br-3ukrb's and br-u5biy's tests may fail, and only identically on base);
  - storage + tools clippy;
  - workspace prodcheck;
  - tools it;
  - conformance.

REPORTED, not gated:
- the br-9ott5 probe at P2;
- fence-contended waits by holder;
- reconciler counters;
- release-artifact refusals;
- reservation p50/p99;
- send p50/p90, with the closed-loop caveat.

DECISION:
- WIN only if M1, M2, G1-G4 and C hold. A WIN lands L2 (storage lib.rs direct-write admission) with this rule and the
  evidence cited.
- br-9ott5 stays open unless its own probe (P2 included) passes.
- LOSS: one line on br-9ott5 and br-kp1in.19; nothing lands.

